{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC21resendOwnVerificationyyYaKF","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resendOwnVerification"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"extendedModule":"AxiamSDK","title":"resendOwnVerification()","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resendOwnVerification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes no address. The server reads it off the caller’s own record, and this signature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately offers no way to name a different one: a parameter here would let an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authenticated session mail an arbitrary address."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" this reports the outcome, because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller is signed in to the account it is asking about and none of the outcomes tells"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it anything it did not already bring with it:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"returns — a token was minted and the mail "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"enqueued"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Delivery is asynchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and can still fail at the provider; a queue that accepts everything in front of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provider that rejects it looks exactly like this succeeding (§25.7 rule 3)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamError.authz"},{"type":"text","text":" (from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"409"},{"type":"text","text":") — already verified, or an account state that must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not be sent a live token."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamError.network"},{"text":" (from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"text":") — the daily resend limit.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§25.7 rule 2 forbids falling back to the unauthenticated endpoint on either failure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and this SDK does not: that fallback turns both back into a silent success and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restores the bug this operation exists to fix, with an extra round trip."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Refused client-side with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no wire call"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when there is no session."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/users\/me\/resend-verification","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (CONTRACT.md §25.1, §25.7) — resend the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"signed-in caller’s own","type":"text"}]},{"text":" verification mail, and say what happened.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits"